    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Buddhism grew from the teaching of Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha, in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the 5th century BCE: suffering arises from craving, and a path of ethics, meditation and insight leads to its end.</li><li>Royal patrons such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>, monks and merchants carried it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, where it took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theravada-buddhism">Theravada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahayana-buddhism">Mahayana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vajrayana">Vajrayana</a> forms.</li><li>It faded from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> after about 1200 but remained a major religion of Asia, was revived in India by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/b-r-ambedkar">B. R. Ambedkar</a> in 1956 and reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> in the 20th century.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The oldest printed book that bears a date is a Buddhist scripture: a copy of the Diamond Sutra, printed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 868 and found in a sealed cave at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunhuang">Dunhuang</a> in 1900.</p></aside>
    </section>

